  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA is clearly the dominant modality (pca_n2000 singleprofile acc=0.485 vs image-only resnet50 acc=0.208), and among tested RNA encoders pca_n2000 outperforms scgpt. However, we have zero data on whether multiprofile aggregation improves over singleprofile—a fundamental design axis that governs a large fraction of the remaining search space. This experiment (config_002) directly tests that question by taking our best-performing configuration (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) and changing only the profile setting to multiprofile with the simplest aggregation (avgpool). It isolates the multiprofile effect while holding the encoder constant, giving a clean comparison to config_001. Choosing avgpool over transformer avoids introducing a second confounding variable; if avgpool already shows a gain, we can then test transformer in a follow-up. Under a tight budget, resolving whether multiprofile is worth pursuing at all is the highest-information next step, as it determines whether the many multiprofile and multimodal-multiprofile configurations are worth further exploration."
}

